# Virtual environments
#
# `venv310/` is the whole-directory ignore: it matches the directory and, because
# it ends with a slash, git never descends into it. Listing its sub-paths
# individually (Lib/, Scripts/, Include/, *.exe, ...) was redundant, and any file
# type added by a future Python/pip release outside that hand-written list would
# have been tracked. One directory rule cannot go stale.
venv/
venv*/
.venv/
.venv*/
ENV/
env/

