# IDE / Editor
#
# Only genuinely machine-local editor state is ignored. The project's own
# `.vscode/settings.json` (Python interpreter, pytest and test paths),
# `.vscode/tasks.json` and `.vscode/extensions.json` are shared development
# configuration referenced by PROJECT_STRUCTURE.md and must stay tracked.
#
# There is deliberately no bare `.vscode/` rule here: because it ends with a
# slash, git never descends into the directory, which would make the
# negations below unreachable and the shared config untrackable. Ignoring the
# directory's *contents* with `.vscode/*` instead keeps the negations working.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/tasks.json
!.vscode/launch.json
extension/.vscode/*
!extension/.vscode/launch.json
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
*.sublime-project
*.sublime-workspace
.project
.pydevproject
.settings/

