# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Extension build artifacts
#
# `extension/backend/` is GENERATED from `backend/` by scripts/sync-backend.js
# and `extension/out/` is GENERATED from `src/` by tsc. Neither is source: edit
# `backend/` and `extension/src/` instead.
#
# The root `*.vsix` is deliberately NOT ignored — it is the installable
# artifact that users download straight from the repository root.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
extension/backend/
extension/out/
extension/dist/
extension/.vscode-test/
extension/out-test/
extension/node_modules/
extension/*.vsix
extension/*.log

# Working copies of the VSIX produced by `npm run package`.
#
# `extension/*.vsix` (above) covers the build directory. The released copy at the
# repository root is deliberately NOT ignored and is NOT version-pinned: an earlier
# `/llm-training-agent-*.vsix` + `!/llm-training-agent-1.0.0.vsix` pair silently
# started ignoring a freshly built 1.0.1 VSIX, which would have shipped a stale
# download link in INSTALLATION_GUIDE.md. Ignoring nothing at the root is correct.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local runtime data (recreated on first start)
#
# The backend stores its SQLite database, WAL and shared-memory index next to
# the running backend (`llm_training_agent.db*`). These are per-machine runtime
# state, never source, and must not be tracked.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Root-level build/test noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.generated.md

